WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:02.575
The agent sends Markdown and a few seconds

2
00:00:02.575 --> 00:00:05.295
later the browser shows narrated slides.

3
00:00:05.295 --> 00:00:08.025
We'll follow that one call through the stdio

4
00:00:08.025 --> 00:00:11.825
shim, the daemon, the builder and the narrator.

5
00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:15.150
The agent speaks MCP over stdio to a

6
00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:16.650
small shim.

7
00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:18.995
The shim forwards the call to the daemon,

8
00:00:18.995 --> 00:00:22.350
which is one long-lived process per machine.

9
00:00:22.545 --> 00:00:25.770
Inside it, the builder turns Markdown into slides,

10
00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:28.950
and the narrator turns their text into speech.

11
00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:31.525
Finally the daemon pushes the result to the

12
00:00:31.525 --> 00:00:32.875
browser.

13
00:00:33.295 --> 00:00:35.945
The agent's tool call lands in the shim,

14
00:00:35.945 --> 00:00:39.295
which looks for daemon.json in the data folder.

15
00:00:39.295 --> 00:00:41.200
If no daemon of the same version is

16
00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:45.750
healthy, it starts showntell serve and waits for /health.

17
00:00:45.895 --> 00:00:48.113
Then the shim's service forwards the call as

18
00:00:48.113 --> 00:00:53.095
an HTTP post to /api/rpc/add,

19
00:00:53.095 --> 00:00:55.550
with the arguments as JSON.

20
00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:57.237
The bearer token

21
00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:04.895
The route compares the token in constant time,

22
00:01:04.895 --> 00:01:07.075
then checks the method name against an allow

23
00:01:07.075 --> 00:01:08.250
list.

24
00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:11.312
It then calls the same method on LocalService

25
00:01:11.312 --> 00:01:14.883
that the HTTP MCP route would call.

26
00:01:14.883 --> 00:01:17.895
A ValueError becomes a 400 with the message,

27
00:01:17.895 --> 00:01:20.675
so the agent sees a plain error.

28
00:01:21.145 --> 00:01:23.900
Session.add first appends the Markdown to the stored

29
00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:24.807
source.

30
00:01:24.807 --> 00:01:27.207
Then the builder parses it into slides,

31
00:01:27.207 --> 00:01:28.820
reads code from disk,

32
00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:32.000
resolves cues and records problems.

33
00:01:32.145 --> 00:01:34.957
Every narration paragraph becomes a new say.

34
00:01:34.957 --> 00:01:37.583
Each one asks the narrator for audio.

35
00:01:37.583 --> 00:01:39.633
The job key is a hash of model,

36
00:01:39.633 --> 00:01:41.995
voice, speed and spoken text,

37
00:01:41.995 --> 00:01:44.700
so a cache hit returns at once.

38
00:01:44.845 --> 00:01:46.962
On a miss, the job joins a queue

39
00:01:46.962 --> 00:01:48.920
ordered by position in the walkthrough,

40
00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:51.795
and one worker thread voices them in turn.

41
00:01:51.795 --> 00:01:54.400
Finally the change is announced.

42
00:01:54.845 --> 00:01:57.145
The daemon sends the reply back at once,

43
00:01:57.145 --> 00:01:58.620
listing problems.

44
00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:00.345
It does not wait for the audio,

45
00:02:00.345 --> 00:02:02.800
so the agent can keep writing.

46
00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:05.070
Voice jobs go to the narrator.

47
00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:06.920
As it finishes each paragraph,

48
00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:09.100
the audio comes back and the daemon marks

49
00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:11.025
that slide changed.

50
00:02:11.145 --> 00:02:14.775
The event stream coalesces changes for fifty milliseconds

51
00:02:14.775 --> 00:02:17.125
and sends only the changed slides plus the

52
00:02:17.125 --> 00:02:18.675
slide order.

53
00:02:18.795 --> 00:02:21.187
The player then fetches the audio and plays

54
00:02:21.187 --> 00:02:22.707
it against its timeline,

55
00:02:22.707 --> 00:02:24.662
so you see a slide appear while the

56
00:02:24.662 --> 00:02:27.375
agent is still writing the next one.

57
00:02:27.795 --> 00:02:30.683
The call returns before the audio exists.

58
00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:32.070
That is the design:

59
00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:33.475
the shim stays thin,

60
00:02:33.475 --> 00:02:35.120
the daemon holds the state,

61
00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:38.075
and the builder gives feedback straight away.

62
00:02:38.195 --> 00:02:40.270
The narrator works in the background,

63
00:02:40.270 --> 00:02:42.788
and the browser receives each slide as soon

64
00:02:42.788 --> 00:02:44.775
as its voice is ready.
